  "id": "methodological-pluralism",
  "term": "methodological pluralism",
  "definition": "Methodological pluralism means that the studies in a body of research use a range of different methods rather than one uniform approach. In this context, it refers to expected variation in how eligible studies were designed, making a narrative summary more suitable than combining findings in a single standardized way.",
